  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The emission spectra of two stars, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> and <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span>, are analyzed. The wavelength of peak spectral intensity for star <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> is observed to be twice that of star <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\lambda_Y = 2\\lambda_X\"></span>). Additionally, star <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> is found to have a total luminosity four times greater than star <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"L_Y = 4L_X\"></span>).</p>\n<p>What is the ratio of the radius of star <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"Y\"></span> to the radius of star <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"X\"></span> (<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{R_Y}{R_X}\"></span>)?</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">2</li><li data-label=\"B\">4</li><li data-label=\"C\">8</li><li data-label=\"D\">16</li></ol>"
  },
